        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Erlend Øye\n- Organizations: Kings of Convenience, Belle and Sebastian, Hjálmar, The Whitest Boy Alive\n- Places: Bergen, Norway, Glasgow, Reykjavík, Seoul, Iceland, Scotland\n- Products: Legao, \"Garota\"\n- Topics: indie folk-pop, solo albums, bands, music videos\n\nFacts:\n- Kings of Convenience is an indie folk-pop duo from Bergen, Norway.\n- Belle and Sebastian is a Scottish band that was formed in Glasgow in January 1996.\n- Legao is the second solo album by Erlend Øye, who is a singer in Kings of Convenience and The Whitest Boy Alive.\n- Legao was recorded in Reykjavík with Hjálmar, a reggae group from Iceland.\n- The single \"Garota\" from Legao was anticipated by a videoclip shot in Seoul.",
